              {row.arm1_pct > 0 && <div class="paired-fill upgrader" style={`width: ${row.arm1_pct}%;`}>
                <span class="paired-val">{row.arm1_pct}%</span>
              </div>}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="paired-row">
            <span class="paired-mini-label">Defectors</span>
            <div class="paired-track">
              {row.arm2_pct > 0 && <div class="paired-fill defector" style={`width: ${row.arm2_pct}%;`}>
                <span class="paired-val">{row.arm2_pct}%</span>
              </div>}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class={`paired-delta ${row.arm2_pct - row.arm1_pct > 0 ? 'pos' : 'neg'}`}>
          {row.arm2_pct - row.arm1_pct > 0 ? '+' : ''}{row.arm2_pct - row.arm1_pct} pp{sigStar(row.p_value)}
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="insight">
    <p><strong>Read:</strong> Three triggers separate the arms at significance: <strong>content-driven discovery</strong> (defectors +42 pp, p&lt;0.001), <strong>product dissatisfaction with the plateau</strong> (upgraders +27 pp, p&lt;0.001), and <strong>visual self-confrontation</strong> (upgraders slightly higher, p=0.05). Multiple-factors-converging is roughly even across both arms; when triggers stack, the brand attachment becomes the deciding variable.</p>
  </div>
